{"amendments":[{"body":"`crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:717-744` builds the redox scenarios with `HarnessRun::from_state(...)`, but `HarnessRun::from_state` only wraps the provided state (`crates/tank_harness/src/lib.rs:462-468`) and `TankState::new()` leaves `source_water_catalog` empty (`crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs:107`). The weekly `WaterChangePercent { source_profile_id: \"moderate\" }` actions therefore fail with `UnknownSourceProfile`, so `probe_substrate_redox_denitrification` aborts before any of its assertions run. Either seed the source-water catalog for these custom states or keep using scenario-based construction for tests that perform water changes.","rationale":"`cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_habitat_geometry_probes -- --nocapture` currently fails here."},{"body":"`crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:246-259` now requires the 2×-media run to finish with at least 95% of the small run's nitrifier biomass, but that proxy is not stable under the current model: the edited test fails with `small=0.0912g, large=0.0761g`. This refactor also stopped measuring the actual cycling behavior in the loop (`crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:211-218`), so the probe is both red and no longer directly validating the \"bigger media cycles faster\" claim in its name.","rationale":"This is a concrete regression in the edited test and weakens the probe's behavioral signal."},{"body":"`crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs:302-325` mutates `TankState::new()` to use 18 cm vs 55 cm fill heights, then only rewrites a subset of dissolved totals. `TankState::new()` had already sized `state.water` for the original default geometry (`crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs:63-79`), so untouched pools such as alkalinity, Ca/Mg, chloride, DOC/DON, etc. are left at default-tank totals and end up at different concentrations in the shallow and deep runs. That means `probe_light_depth_shallow_vs_deep_growth` is not isolating depth/light anymore; part of the observed divergence can come from stale chemistry that was never rescaled to the new volume.","rationale":"This makes a passing probe scientifically confounded and less robust."}],"summary":"Reviewed the diff and ran `cargo test -p tank_harness --test e2e_habitat_geometry_probes -- --nocapture`. Two edited probes are currently failing (`probe_substrate_redox_denitrification` and `probe_biofilter_scaling_bigger_media_faster_cycling`), and the light-depth probe now compares states whose chemistry was not fully rescaled after manual geometry changes."}